 Options are: - tired; - happy; - relieved; - peaceful; - excited; - stressed; - surprised; - anxious;
I zip up my bag before leaving. I feel peaceful.

The act of zipping up a bag is often associated with preparation for travel or departure. Among the emotions listed, "peaceful" is the most appropriate choice because it reflects a state of calmness and tranquility, which is consistent with the action of zipping up a bag. This action typically indicates that one is ready to leave, and being prepared can bring a sense of peace and contentment.
